/* 段落记忆 · 词层 4 · 子块 c：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(4,{"sub":"c","par":{"mould":{"tw":[["moulding",4],["form",3],["chip",3],["dish",2],["slime",6],["shape",2],["hill",3],["soil",2],["chisel",6],["work",0]],"en":"On a wet hill above the village, an old potter would work with clay all day. He first pressed the soft soil into a rough shape, then set it in a wooden mould. A thin chisel helped him cut a fine moulding along the edge of every dish. Once a green slime grew on the walls of his shed, because the air there was never dry. A careless knock could chip a finished plate, so he moved slowly and spoke little. His hands gave each piece the same simple form. The clay, he said, remembers the shape of the hands that made it.","zh":"村子上方那座湿润的小山上，一位老陶工整天都在跟泥打交道。他先把松软的泥土压出一个大概的形状，再放进木模子里。一把薄薄的凿子帮他把每只盘子的边缘修出一道细线脚。有一回他棚子的墙上长出了一层绿黏苔，因为那儿从没干过。稍微磕一下就能把盘子磕出个豁口，所以他动作很慢，话也不多。他的双手让每一件东西都有同样朴素的形。他说，泥会记住做它的那双手的形状。"},"multiply":{"tw":[["multiple",4],["breed",3],["double",3],["increase",2],["divide",1],["subtract",6],["reproduce",2],["raise",3],["proliferate",6],["manifold",0]],"en":"In the school garden we kept a pair of rabbits, and soon they began to multiply. Within a month their number would double, and then increase again, because rabbits breed so quickly. The teacher asked us to divide the total by two and then subtract the ones we had given away. Our answers were multiple, and none of them matched hers. She said that living things reproduce in ways that can proliferate faster than any sum on paper. A student raised a good question: how many could one pair produce in a year? The garden taught us more than a whole term in the classroom, and the reasons were manifold.","zh":"在学校的小园子里，我们养了一对兔子，没多久它们就开始繁殖。不到一个月，数量就翻一倍，接着又往上加，因为兔子生得太快。老师让我们把总数除以二，再减去送人的那几只。我们算出了好几种答案，没有一个跟她的一样。她说，活物的繁育能比纸上任何算式扩增得都快。一个学生提了个好问题：一对兔子一年能生出多少只？这座小园子教给我们的，比教室里一整个学期还多，而其中的道理是多方面的。"},"pursuit":{"tw":[["pursue",4],["chase",0],["stalk",3],["search",2],["aim",6],["quest",0],["motion",2],["race",6],["pastime",2]],"en":"For my uncle, bird watching is a quiet pursuit that fills every free weekend. He will pursue a rare bird for hours, moving with slow, careful motion. His aim is never to catch it, only to see it once. He would stalk along the river bank, then stop and listen to the search of the wind in the reeds. Last year he joined a race to list the most species in one month, a friendly quest among old friends. Sometimes he will chase a shadow for half a day and come home with nothing at all. Still he says it is the best pastime he knows.","zh":"对我叔叔来说，观鸟是一种安静的爱好，占满了他每一个空闲的周末。为了一只稀有的鸟，他会守上几个钟头，动作缓慢而小心。他的目的从不是捉住它，只是看一眼。他会沿着河岸悄悄跟过去，然后停下来，听风在芦苇里搜寻的动静。去年他参加了一场比谁一个月记下的鸟种多的比赛，是老朋友之间的一次友好追寻。有时他追着一道影子跑上半天，回家时两手空空。可他说，这是他最中意的消遣。"},"irritate":{"tw":[["bother",0],["rub",3],["stimulate",2],["soothe",1],["infuriate",6],["annoy",0],["harass",3],["displease",2],["frown",6],["devil",0]],"en":"A small rash on my arm began to irritate me for a whole week. It would bother me at night, and I could not stop rubbing it. A loud noise from the street would infuriate me even more. My sister said I should not let small things annoy me, but she was not the one with an itchy arm. The cream did soothe the skin for an hour or so. The doctor explained that dust can harass the skin and stimulate the rash, and that heat would displease the nerves. Her frown told me to stop scratching. In the end the little devil left, and I slept again.","zh":"胳膊上一小片疹子让我难受了整整一星期。夜里它来烦我，我忍不住一直去搓。街上一点响动都能把我惹得更火。姐姐说我不该被小事烦着，可她胳膊上又没痒。药膏确实让皮肤舒服了个把钟头。医生说，灰尘会刺激皮肤、把疹子激发起来，热也会让神经难受。她皱了下眉，意思是别再抓了。最后那个小讨厌鬼走了，我也总算睡了个好觉。"},"obstruct":{"tw":[["block",0],["check",3],["hide",2],["free",1],["thwart",6],["embarrass",0],["hang",3],["prevent",2],["expedite",6],["jam",0]],"en":"A broken truck would obstruct the narrow road every morning and make the traffic jam worse. The driver tried to hide the problem from the police, which only served to embarrass him later. A young officer had to check the papers and prevent anyone from passing on the wrong side. Two neighbours came out to thwart the plan of a man who wanted to push ahead of the queue. The road was not free until noon. A long banner would hang over the gate and block the view of the corner. The council promised to expedite the repairs before winter.","zh":"每天早上都有一辆坏了的卡车堵住那条窄路，让本来就堵的车流更堵。司机想把事情瞒着警察，结果只是让自己更难堪。一名年轻警员只好查证件，不让人从错误的一侧挤过去。两个邻居出来拦住了那个想插队抢先的人。直到中午路才空出来。一条长横幅挂在门口，遮住了拐角的视线。镇里答应在入冬前加快修好这条路。"},"originate":{"tw":[["origin",4],["grow",0],["head",3],["begin",2],["migrate",6],["rise",0],["exist",6],["start",0]],"en":"Many of the birds that nest here originate from a warmer land in the south. Their long journey will begin in the autumn and end in the spring. They migrate along the same line every year, following the head of the valley. The river that feeds our fields would rise from a small spring in the hills. Nobody knows how long that spring has been there, or how long the birds have existed. The origin of the valley's life seems to be that single spring. In dry years the trees do not grow as tall, and the whole season can start late.","zh":"在这儿筑巢的许多鸟，都是从南边更暖的地方来的。它们漫长的旅程在秋天开始，到春天结束。每年它们沿着同一条线迁徙，顺着山谷的上头飞。滋养我们田地的这条河，就是从山间一眼小泉里涌出来的。没人知道那眼泉存在了多久，也没人知道这些鸟已经在这里活了多久。这片谷地里一切的由来，似乎就是那一汪泉水。碰上旱年，树也长不了那么高。"},"indulge":{"tw":[["spoil",0],["spree",3],["treat",2],["flirt",6],["gratify",0],["wallow",3],["provide",2],["partake",6],["pamper",0]],"en":"During the winter holidays my aunt likes to indulge her grandchildren a little. She will spoil them with sweets and provide a warm treat for every visitor. One long shopping spree can empty her purse in a single afternoon. She does not want to pamper them too much, she says, but she cannot help it. Her aim is simply to gratify a small wish and see them smile. The children will wallow in the new toys for a week. She would never flirt with the idea of a strict rule. All of us partake in the fun.","zh":"寒假里，姑妈爱稍微纵着点孙子孙女。她用糖果惯着他们，还给每个上门的人都备一份热乎乎的吃食。一趟长长的采购，一下午就能把她的钱包掏空。她说不想太娇惯孩子，可就是忍不住。她的心思很简单：满足一个小愿望，看他们笑一笑。孩子们会在新玩具里赖上一个星期。她绝不会拿定规矩的念头开玩笑。我们也全都跟着凑这份热闹。"},"infer":{"tw":[["guess",0],["tell",3],["reason",2],["presume",6],["understand",0],["elicit",3],["solve",2],["correlate",6],["derive",0]],"en":"From a single footprint in the mud, a good student can infer a great deal. She may guess the size of the walker and tell the direction of the step. A careful reason can help her understand what happened an hour before. She must not presume too much from one small mark. Her teacher would elicit answers from the class and let them solve the puzzle together. They tried to correlate the time with the shape of the print. The whole method seemed to derive from simple watching and a great deal of patience.","zh":"从泥地里一个脚印，好学生就能推断出不少东西。她可以猜出走路人的身量，还能说出这一步朝哪个方向。仔细想一想，就能帮她明白一小时前发生了什么。她不能凭一个小印记就料定太多。老师会从学生嘴里一句句问出答案，让大家一起把这道谜解开。他们试着把时间和印子的形状对上关系。这整套办法，看着就是从老老实实地观察里来的。"},"jazz":{"tw":[["bed",0],["swing",3],["play",2],["music",6],["love",0],["funk",3],["talk",2],["folk",6],["wind",0]],"en":"On a warm evening my uncle would play jazz on an old radio in his small room. A slow swing would fill the house and keep his feet moving. He would talk about the singers he loved when he was young. His music of choice was never folk or funk, though he liked both well enough. When the window was open, a soft wind carried the sound into the street. He would sit on the bed with his eyes closed and listen. For him the best evening ended with one quiet tune.","zh":"天暖的晚上，叔叔会在小屋里用一台旧收音机放爵士。慢悠悠的摇摆节奏填满整栋房子，他的脚也跟着动。他会讲起年轻时喜欢的那些歌手。他偏爱的从不是民谣或放克，虽然这两种他也都爱听。窗户一开，一阵软软的风就把声音送到街上。他会坐在床上，闭着眼听。对他来说，最好的夜晚以一支安静的曲子收尾。"},"lap":{"tw":[["wash",0],["tongue",3],["drink",2],["pole",6],["circle",0],["cuff",3],["lie",2],["finish",6],["circuit",0]],"en":"In the evening our old cat would lie on my lap by the window. She would wash her face and let her tongue clean each paw. After a long drink she would walk in a slow circle before she slept. A tall pole near the door was her favourite place to watch the birds. I would roll up my cuff and stroke her back. She could finish a whole bowl of milk without a pause. One full circuit of the garden in the last light, and she was ready for bed.","zh":"傍晚，我们那只老猫会趴在窗边我的腿上。它洗洗脸，用舌头把每只爪子舔干净。喝足了水，它先慢慢转一圈才睡。门边那根高杆子是它看鸟最中意的地方。我卷起袖口，摸摸它的背。一碗奶它一口气就能喝完。在园子里绕完一整圈，它就准备去睡了。"},"leaf":{"tw":[["flip",0],["page",3],["grow",2],["yellow",6],["flick",0],["pad",3],["section",2],["tree",6],["thumb",0]],"en":"In the library a dry leaf fell out of an old book and landed on my pad. I would flip the page and find the same shape pressed flat inside. The yellow colour showed how many years it had been there. Under the tall tree outside, new leaves begin to grow every April. I would flick the corner of the cover and read the next section. My thumb kept the place while I looked for a pen. The book was due back on Friday, and I wanted one more quiet hour with it.","zh":"在图书馆里，一片干叶子从一本旧书里掉出来，落在我的本子上。我翻过一页，发现同样的形状被压扁了夹在里面。那发黄的颜色说明它在那儿待了不少年头。窗外那棵大树下，每年四月都有新叶长出来。我用指头弹了一下封面的角，接着读下一节。找笔的时候，我用拇指压着那儿没让书合上。这本书周五要还。"},"lick":{"tw":[["work",0],["answer",3],["beat",2],["wash",6],["bat",0],["break",3],["blow",2],["fork",6],["punch",0]],"en":"My little brother would lick the spoon and then ask for the whole bowl. My mother had to work fast and answer his endless questions at the same time. When he wanted more, he would beat the table with a bat he kept as a toy. A light blow of wind came through the open window and lifted the paper on the table. He would wash his hands only after a promise of cake, and once he used a fork to chase a piece across his plate. One wrong punch at the dough broke the shape of the loaf. Still, the kitchen was the happiest room in the house.","zh":"小弟弟舔完勺子，就伸手要整碗。母亲一边得手脚麻利地干活，一边还要应付他没完没了的问题。他还想要，就拿那根当玩具的棒子敲桌子。一阵轻风从开着的窗子进来，把桌上的纸吹了起来。只有答应给他蛋糕，他才肯洗手；有一回他还用叉子追着盘子上的一块跑。他往面团上乱捶了一下，把面包的形状打坏了。可厨房依旧是这屋里最快活的地方。"},"linger":{"tw":[["lounge",0],["prowl",3],["leave",2],["rush",1],["erupt",6],["hover",0],["move",2],["dissipate",6],["lurk",0]],"en":"After the guests had gone, a warm smell of coffee would linger in the kitchen. Nobody wanted to leave the table, so we would lounge in our chairs and talk. A cat began to prowl along the wall and lurk behind the door. In the street a few cars would hover near the corner and then move away. When the wind rose, the smoke would dissipate into the night air. Laughter could erupt from the next room for no reason at all. We had no rush and no plan for the rest of the night.","zh":"客人走了之后，厨房里还留着咖啡的温热气味。谁也不想离开桌子，我们就靠在椅子上聊。一只猫沿着墙根溜达，又蹲在门后不动了。街上几辆车在拐角那儿盘桓了一阵，然后开走了。风一起，烟就散进夜色里。隔壁屋里会无缘无故地爆出一阵笑。我们不赶时间，也没什么打算。"},"lounge":{"tw":[["couch",0],["prowl",3],["room",2],["inn",6],["linger",0],["settee",3],["seat",2],["garage",6],["lurk",0]],"en":"Last summer we stayed at a small inn near the coast, and its lounge became our favourite place. I would linger there after dinner, sitting on a soft settee with a cup of tea. My sister chose the old couch by the window, while our dog liked to prowl around the quiet room. A thin cat used to lurk behind the door and watch us from its hidden seat. One evening we heard a car stop in the garage below, and a guest came up to rest. Nobody wanted to leave that warm room, so we stayed until the lamps went dim. Even now I can picture the long couch and the gentle light.","zh":"去年夏天我们住在海边一家小旅店，它的大堂吧成了我们最爱待的地方。晚饭后我总爱在那儿流连，捧杯茶坐在软沙发上。我妹妹挑窗边那张旧长沙发，我们的狗则喜欢在安静的房间里转来转去。一只瘦猫常常躲在门后，从它藏身的位置盯着我们。有天傍晚，我们听见楼下车库停了辆车，一位客人上来歇脚。谁都不想离开那间暖屋子，一直待到灯变暗。直到现在，我还能想起那张长沙发和柔和的光。"},"obscure":{"tw":[["apart",0],["overshadow",3],["change",2],["familiar",6],["dark",0],["mystify",3],["reduce",2],["subject",6],["hide",2]],"en":"In the archive I found an obscure map that no one had studied for years. Its lines were dark and faint, and the names on it seemed to hide behind a strange code. The symbols would mystify anyone who was not familiar with the region. To make sense of it, I had to reduce every mark to a simple shape and keep the pages apart on the table. My teacher said the subject was hard and that the plan's details were obscure, so she asked for a careful rewrite. We had to change one old word that could overshadow the rest. Slowly the dark picture became clear, and the map no longer hid its secrets.","zh":"在档案馆里，我找到一张多年无人研究的模糊地图。上面的线条又暗又淡，那些名字像是躲在一套奇怪的暗号后面。不熟悉这一带的人，会被那些符号弄得一头雾水。为了弄懂它，我只好把每个记号简化成一个形状，再把纸页摊开在桌上。老师说这个题目很难，而且那份方案的细节很晦涩，所以要我认真重写一遍。我们得改掉一个会盖过其余部分的旧词。慢慢地，那幅昏暗的图变得清晰起来，地图也不再藏着自己的秘密了。"},"offset":{"tw":[["first",0],["threshold",3],["balance",2],["decline",6],["start",0],["counteract",3],["print",2],["surge",6],["branch",0]],"en":"When the small print shop opened its first branch, the manager had to balance the books every week. At the start, sales would decline, and a sudden surge in paper prices hit them hard. To counteract that loss, they began to print a cheap leaflet for nearby cafes. The owner hoped the new orders would offset the higher cost of paper. He kept a written threshold for spending, so nothing would run wild. It was the first time they had faced such a drop, and every branch felt it. Slowly the numbers settled, and the shop found its balance again.","zh":"这家小印刷店开出第一家分店时，经理每周都得把账目摆平。起初，销量下滑，纸张价格又突然猛涨，把他们打得够呛。为了抵消这笔损失，他们开始为附近的咖啡馆印一种便宜的小传单。老板希望新来的订单能抵消纸张上涨的成本。他给开支定了一条书面的门槛，免得事情失控。那是他们头一回碰上这样的下跌，每家分店都感受到了。慢慢地，数字稳住了，小店又找回了平衡。"},"orbit":{"tw":[["field",0],["front",3],["circle",2],["earth",6],["reach",0],["sweep",3],["path",2],["shuttle",6],["range",0]],"en":"At the science centre a guide explained how a small shuttle would orbit the earth. A wide screen showed its path as a bright circle above the field of clouds. The craft had to reach a height where the pull of the earth grew weak. Each sweep around the planet took about ninety minutes, and the range of its signal covered half a continent. The guide stood at the front and asked us to picture the shuttle as a stone on a string. Once the engines stopped, it would keep moving on that same orbit for years. We left the room with a new sense of how small our world really is.","zh":"在科技馆里，一位讲解员给我们讲一艘小航天飞机怎样绕地球飞行。一块宽屏幕把它明亮的圆形轨道显示在云层之上。飞船必须升到某个高度，那里地球的引力已经变弱。它每绕行星一圈大约要九十分钟，信号的覆盖范围横跨半个大陆。讲解员站在前面，让我们把航天飞机想象成拴在绳子上的石头。一旦引擎停下，它还会沿着同一条轨道飞好几年。走出展厅时，我们才真正感到世界有多小。"},"outfit":{"tw":[["fit",0],["wire",3],["gear",2],["hat",6],["kit",0],["commission",3],["supply",2],["club",6],["rig",0]],"en":"Before the climb, our club met to check every piece of gear we would need. The leader said the outfit for a cold ridge must fit well, so we tried each hat and coat. In the kit there was a small wire cutter, a lamp, and a first-aid pack. We had to rig the ropes carefully and lay out the whole supply on the floor. A new member asked how the shop got its commission for the rented boots. No one could guess, so we simply checked the list twice. By evening everyone was ready, and the club was proud of its team.","zh":"爬山前，我们俱乐部碰头，检查要用的每一件装备。领队说，走寒冷山脊的行头必须合身，于是我们把每顶帽子和外套都试了一遍。工具包里有一把小钢丝钳、一盏灯和一个急救包。我们得把绳子仔细地绑好，再把全部补给摊在地板上。一位新成员问，店里出租登山靴能拿多少佣金。谁也说不准，我们只好把清单又核对了一遍。到傍晚，大家都准备好了，俱乐部也为自己的队伍感到自豪。"},"penetrate":{"tw":[["bottom",0],["cut",3],["enter",2],["porous",6],["dawn",0],["strike",3],["join",2],["enemy",6],["click",0]],"en":"At dawn the photographer tried to penetrate the thick fog that filled the valley. She wanted to enter the old cave at the bottom of the hill before the light grew strong. Her boots sank into the porous rock, which had been worn down by rain for years. A thin beam of light began to strike the wet wall and cut through the grey air. She waited for the right moment, then heard the click of her camera. Later a friend would join her and help carry the heavy bag. Time was the real enemy that morning, because the perfect light never lasts long.","zh":"天刚亮，摄影师就想穿透山谷里浓浓的雾。她想趁光线还不强，走进山脚下那座旧山洞。她的靴子陷进疏松的岩石里，那是被雨水长年磨出来的。一道细细的光开始打上湿墙，把灰色的空气切开。她等着合适的时机，随后听见相机咔嚓一声。稍后会有朋友来与她会合，帮她背那个沉包。那天早上，真正的敌人是时间，因为绝好的光从来留不久。"},"pinch":{"tw":[["catch",0],["tail",3],["steal",2],["pitch",6],["lift",0],["goose",3],["bite",2],["huff",6],["top",0]],"en":"On my uncle's farm a white goose liked to steal grain from the open bag. Every morning I would try to catch it, but the bird was quick and always slipped away. Once it turned and tried to bite my hand, then ran off with a loud huff. I used a long stick to lift the heavy sack and gave the grain a pinch of salt to keep it dry. The goose stood on the top of a small wall and waved its tail like a flag. My uncle laughed and told me not to pitch my hopes too high. In the end we simply built a better gate.","zh":"在我叔叔的农场上，一只白鹅总爱从敞开的袋子里偷谷子。每天早上我都想抓住它，可这鸟动作快，总能溜掉。有一次它转过身想咬我的手，然后气呼呼地跑开了。我用一根长棍挑起那个沉袋子，又往谷子里捏了一小撮盐防潮。那只鹅站在一堵矮墙顶上，尾巴像旗子一样摆来摆去。叔叔笑着叫我别把指望定得太高。最后我们干脆修了一道更结实的门。"},"plague":{"tw":[["harass",0],["needle",3],["annoy",2],["epidemic",6],["pest",0],["torment",3],["afflict",2],["smallpox",6],["blight",0]],"en":"The old plague story still frightens visitors in the small museum. A guide told us how an epidemic once swept through the town and began to afflict every street. Few families escaped, and a terrible blight fell on the market. Doctors of that time knew nothing of smallpox or other germs, and their needles could not help. Fleas and other pests would torment the sick and harass the poor even more. It was hard not to feel that such suffering would annoy anyone who heard it. At the end the guide reminded us that clean water and care kept later plagues away.","zh":"在这个小博物馆里，那个关于瘟疫的老故事依旧让参观者害怕。讲解员讲起一场时疫如何席卷全城，开始折磨每一条街。几乎没有人家幸免，集市也遭到一场可怕的摧残。那时的医生对天花之类的病菌一无所知，他们的针也帮不上忙。跳蚤和其他害虫折磨病人，更让穷人苦不堪言。听到这些，谁心里都会觉得难受。最后讲解员提醒我们，干净的水和照料让后来的瘟疫没有再回来。"},"plunge":{"tw":[["dive",0],["duck",3],["drop",2],["tumble",6],["dump",0],["soak",3],["concentrate",2],["rise",6],["absorb",0]],"en":"On the first warm day of June, my cousin decided to plunge into the cold pool. She took a deep breath, watched the water, and made a clean dive from the low board. Then she would duck under the surface and soak her hair until it was heavy. A sudden drop in the wind made her tumble once, but she laughed and stood up. The coach told her to concentrate on her legs and let the water absorb each push. Slowly she began to rise through the blue and reach the far wall. Someone had to dump a bucket of warm water at the edge to keep her from shivering.","zh":"六月里第一个暖和的日子，我表妹决定一头扎进冰凉的泳池。她深吸一口气，看了看水面，从低板上干净利落地跳了下去。接着她潜到水下，把头发泡得沉甸甸的。风里忽然一阵转凉，让她打了个趔趄，可她笑着站了起来。教练让她把注意力放在腿上，让水吸收每一次蹬力。她慢慢从蓝色里浮起来，够到了对面的池壁。有人只好在池边倒了一桶温水，免得她发抖。"},"poke":{"tw":[["dig",0],["hook",3],["bag",2],["shove",6],["nose",0],["jab",3],["blow",2],["prick",6],["pound",0]],"en":"My father showed me how to poke a sharp hook through the soft bait. I had to dig in the little bag for the right piece and then jab it on firmly. The wind gave the boat a hard shove, and I nearly fell onto the wet floor. A stray branch could prick my arm if I was not careful, so I kept my sleeve down. Father blew on his hands, took a slow breath, and gave the water a light blow with the net. Once a fish pulled hard, his heart began to pound. Later a thin bird poked its long nose into the weeds and stole our bait.","zh":"父亲教我怎么把锋利的鱼钩穿过软饵。我得在小袋子里翻出合适的一小块，再牢牢地扎上去。一阵风把船猛推了一下，我差点摔在湿漉漉的甲板上。要是不小心，一根乱枝会扎到我的胳膊，所以我把袖子拉得低低的。父亲朝手上哈了口气，慢慢吸了口气，用网朝水面轻轻一拨。有条鱼猛地一拽，他的心就怦怦直跳。后来一只瘦鸟把长鼻子伸进草丛，偷走了我们的饵。"},"rack":{"tw":[["stand",0],["bleed",3],["cut",2],["dough",6],["wheel",0],["barbecue",3],["draw",2],["refrigerator",6],["squeeze",0]],"en":"In the small bakery, the cook kept every loaf on a tall rack near the window. She would stand there at five in the morning and cut the cold dough into even pieces. A rolling wheel helped her draw the flat shapes, and she had to squeeze each one into the right size. Once she cut her thumb on a sharp edge and watched it bleed for a moment. Near the refrigerator stood a tiny barbecue she used to toast the tops. Every morning the same work, and yet she loved the quiet of it. By ten the rack was full and the shop smelled warm.","zh":"在这家小面包房里，厨子把每一炉面包都放在窗边高高的架子上。她每天清晨五点站在那儿，把冰凉的面团切成均匀的小块。一个滚轮帮她画出扁平的形状，她得把每一块都捏到合适的大小。有一次她在锋利的边上割到拇指，看着它流了一会儿血。冰箱旁边放着一台小烤架，她用它把面包顶部烤上色。每天都是同样的活，可她就喜欢这份安静。到十点，架子已经放满，店里一片暖香。"},"refine":{"tw":[["complicate",0],["involve",3],["better",2],["calibrate",6],["polish",0],["develop",3],["change",2],["enrich",6],["elaborate",0]],"en":"My cousin works in a small coffee workshop where she has to refine every batch by taste. At first the job would involve long hours, and one wrong step could complicate the whole process. She had to calibrate the machine each morning and watch the colour of the beans. To make a better cup, she would polish the old grinder and change the water filter often. The owner asked her to develop a new blend and to enrich it with a light, sweet note. She would elaborate on every choice for customers who asked. Over a year her skill grew, and the shop's name grew with it.","zh":"我表姐在一家小咖啡作坊干活，每一批豆子她都得靠味觉去精制。一开始，这活要花很长时间，一步出错就会把整个流程弄复杂。她每天早上都得校准机器，盯着豆子的颜色。为了做出更好的一杯，她会把旧磨盘擦亮，还常常换水滤芯。老板让她开发一款新拼配，并用一缕清甜的香气加以丰富。有顾客发问，她就会把每个选择细细讲开。一年下来，她的手艺长了，这家店的名气也跟着长了。"},"infinite":{"tw":[["infinity",4],["space",0],["attribute",2],["finite",1],["dimension",6],["myriad",0],["tangent",6]],"en":"In the night class the teacher said the universe may be infinite, and she talked about infinity and the size of space. She said the stars look like a myriad of small lights in one wide dimension. It is hard to hold such an idea in the head, because our own lives are finite. Out of this, she went off on a tangent about an old poem. She would attribute the beauty of the sky to light that has travelled for ages. A plain drawing on the board helped us picture what no eye can reach. When the bell rang, nobody wanted to leave.","zh":"在夜校课上，老师讲起了无限和太空的大小。她说，星星看起来就像无边的太空里数不清的小灯。这样的想法很难在脑子里装下，因为我们自己的生命是有限的。说着说着，她扯到了一个旧诗句上。她总把天空的美归因于走了千万年的光。黑板上一个朴素的图示，帮我们想象肉眼看不到的东西。铃响时，谁都不想走。"},"magnitude":{"tw":[["magnify",4],["degree",3],["property",2],["earthquake",6],["order",3],["importance",2],["scale",6]],"en":"The morning news told of an earthquake far away and its surprising magnitude. Reporters tried to magnify the story, but the facts were already serious enough. To some degree people near the coast felt the ground move for a few seconds. A strong quake can damage any property, whether a small house or a tall block. The order of the streets had been broken, and rescue teams moved in at once. Experts put the event on a large scale and stressed its importance for future planning. By noon aid was already on its way.","zh":"早间新闻播报了远方的一场地震，以及它惊人的震级。记者们想把这件事渲染得更大，可事实本身已经足够严重。海岸附近的人，多少都感到地面晃动了几秒。强震能损坏任何房产，无论是一间小屋还是一栋高楼。街道的秩序被打乱，救援队立刻赶了进去。专家把这次事件放在一个大尺度上看，强调它对将来规划的重要性。到中午，援助已经在路上了。"},"mock":{"tw":[["mockery",4],["tease",3],["treat",2],["elaborate",6],["deride",3],["imitate",2],["assault",6]],"en":"A group of older students began to mock the new boy for his old, torn shoes. They would tease him every day and imitate the way he spoke. Such mockery can feel like a quiet assault on a child's pride. One girl chose to treat him kindly and walked with him all the way to the gate. She told him that those who deride others often fear being alone. He learned to hold his head up and not elaborate on his troubles. By spring the two of them were the very best of friends.","zh":"一群高年级学生开始拿新来的男孩那双旧鞋取笑他。他们天天戏弄他，还模仿他说话的样子。这样的讥笑，对孩子自尊心来说像是一种无声的伤害。有个女孩选择善待他，一路陪他走到大门口。她告诉他，贬低别人的人，往往害怕自己孤单。他学会了抬起头，不再多讲自己的难处。到春天，他们俩成了最要好的朋友。"},"necessity":{"tw":[["necessitate",4],["necessary",4],["need",3],["imperative",6],["essential",0],["importance",6],["requisite",0]],"en":"When the family shop lost its best customer, a change became a real necessity. It was necessary to look at every cost, from rent to the smallest bill. The owner said it was imperative that they find a new market before winter. Even a small repair would necessitate a careful look at the books. Clean shelves and a kind word are essential, but they are not the whole story. He stressed the importance of the need to act quickly and well. A licence, once a mere requisite, now seemed like the only key to everything.","zh":"家里的小店失去最好的老主顾后，改变真的成了一种必需。必须把每一项开支都过一遍，从房租到最小的一笔账。老板说，他们务必在入冬前找到新市场。哪怕修一处小地方，也得仔细看看账本。干净的货架和一句好话固然重要，但并不说明一切。他强调，眼下最要紧的是尽快把事办好。那张过去只是必备手续的执照，现在倒像是打开一切的钥匙。"},"nutrition":{"tw":[["nutritious",4],["sustenance",0],["dish",3],["food",2],["hygiene",6],["science",2],["health",6]],"en":"At the school cafeteria the cook tried to give every child good nutrition. She said a nutritious dish does not have to cost much to be good. Rice, beans, and fresh greens were her idea of real sustenance. Clean hands and a tidy kitchen were part of good hygiene, she told us. The science of food had taught her which meals keep a young body strong. She watched the children's health and changed the menu when winter came. A warm lunch, she said, is the very best gift a school can give.","zh":"在学校食堂里，这位厨子尽量让每个孩子都吃得有营养。她说，一道有营养的菜，不一定非要花很多钱。米饭、豆子和新鲜青菜，就是她心里真正的养料。她告诉我们，干净的双手和整洁的厨房都是卫生的一部分。饮食这门学问让她明白，哪些饭菜能让年轻的身体强壮。她留意孩子们的康健，入冬就换菜单。她说，一顿热饭，是学校能给的最好的礼物。"},"inhibit":{"tw":[["suppress",2],["silence",3],["control",2],["modulate",6],["conquer",0],["restrain",3],["bind",6],["curb",0]],"en":"During his first month at the studio, my cousin learned to inhibit every bad habit. He would suppress a laugh when a singer made a small mistake. To keep the session calm, he had to silence his phone and control his temper. His job was to modulate the sound so that no note stood out too loud. Fear can bind a young player, he said, and it will curb the best ideas. He tried to restrain himself from rushing the band. 'You must conquer your own nerves first,' he told me. By the last week he looked calm and sure.","zh":"在录音棚的头一个月，我表弟学会了克制自己的每一个坏毛病。歌手出点小错时，他会忍住不笑。为了让整场录制保持平静，他得把手机静音，还得管住脾气。他的活儿是调节声音，别让哪个音冒得太高。他说，害怕会捆住一个年轻乐手，也会压住最好的想法。他努力约束自己，不催着乐队赶。他对我说，'你得先战胜自己的紧张。'到最后一星期，他看着又稳又定。"},"jar":{"tw":[["shock",0],["vase",3],["blow",2],["cake",6],["clash",0],["move",2],["tray",6],["jolt",0]],"en":"On a busy Saturday the young waiter tried to move a heavy tray of glasses. A tall vase stood too near the edge, and one small jar of honey sat beside it. When he turned, the tray hit the shelf with a loud clash. The jar fell to the floor and broke, which gave everyone a shock. The cook felt a hard blow on her foot but was not badly hurt. She had to place a fresh cake on the good tray and start again. The whole kitchen seemed to jolt for a second, then grew calm. Nobody moved until the last piece was swept away.","zh":"一个忙碌的周六，年轻的侍者想搬动一大盘玻璃杯。一只高花瓶靠边缘太近，旁边还放着一小罐蜂蜜。他一转身，托盘撞在架子上，发出一声刺耳的碰响。罐子掉到地上摔碎了，把大家都吓了一跳。厨师脚上挨了重重一记，幸好人没大碍。她只好换一个好托盘，重新摆上一块新蛋糕。整个厨房仿佛晃了一下，随后又平静下来。最后一片碎片扫走之前，谁也没动。"},"lace":{"tw":[["spike",0],["splice",3],["change",2],["satin",6],["braid",0],["tie",2],["skirt",6],["fortify",0]],"en":"In her small shop a tailor was preparing a dress for a spring wedding. She would splice two lengths of old lace so the pattern looked whole. With a fine needle she added a thin satin band along the waist. The skirt needed a new line of lace, and she chose to change the shade a little. To fortify the edge she sewed it twice, once above and once below. She would braid a small ribbon into the neck and tie it in a bow. A silver spike held the cloth flat while she worked. By evening the dress was ready, and she smiled at it.","zh":"在她那间小店里，一位裁缝正在准备一件春天婚礼的礼服。她把两段旧花边接起来，让花纹看着浑然一体。她用细针在腰上缝了一条薄缎带。裙子需要一道新的花边，她决定把颜色改淡一点。为了给边加固，她缝了两遍，上面一道、下面一道。她要把一条小丝带编进领口，再打个蝴蝶结。一枚银别针把布压平，好让她干活。到傍晚，礼服做好了，她对着它笑了。"},"lever":{"tw":[["prize",0],["key",3],["bar",2],["brake",6],["pry",0],["stick",3],["machine",2],["wheel",6]],"en":"Last winter the wheel of our old car froze, and we had to fix it in the cold garage. My uncle used a long lever to pry the bent part away from the frame. He slipped a metal bar under the edge and pushed with all his weight. A wooden stick helped him hold the brake line out of the way. The whole machine was old, but the engine still ran well. He said the prize was not the car but the lesson it taught. Then he could not find the key, so I had to fetch a spare. By dark the job was done, and we drove home slowly.","zh":"去年冬天，我们那辆旧车的轮子冻住了，只好在冷冰冰的车库里修。叔叔用一根长杠杆把弯掉的那块撬开，离开车架。他把一根铁棒塞到边下，使上全身的劲。一根木棍帮他顶开刹车管线。这台机器老了，可发动机还能好好转。他说，奖赏不是这辆车，而是它教给他的道理。然后他找不到钥匙了，我只好去拿备用的那把。天黑前活干完了，我们慢慢开车回家。"},"loop":{"tw":[["curl",0],["band",3],["tie",2],["curve",6],["coil",0],["noose",3],["wind",2],["parallel",6]],"en":"On the boat every rope must be kept in a tidy loop. My father would wind a long line around his arm, then lay a neat curl on the deck. He taught me to tie a strong knot before the sea grew rough. The heavy coil of rope looked like a wide band on the floor. A second line was laid parallel to the first so the sail would hold. Once I made the shape of a noose by mistake, and he laughed and fixed it. The curve of the rope against the wood was almost pretty. Then we pulled the sail up and left the harbour.","zh":"在船上，每根绳子都得盘成整整齐齐的一圈。父亲会把长绳绕在胳膊上，然后在甲板上放下一卷漂亮的圈。他教我在海上变天前打好一个结实的结。那卷沉甸甸的绳子搁在地上，像一条宽宽的带子。第二根绳跟第一根平行着放，张起的帆才撑得住。有一次我打了个活扣，他笑着帮我改了过来。绳子贴在木头上那道弯，几乎有些好看。然后我们扯起帆，驶离了港口。"},"mist":{"tw":[["cloud",0],["overshadow",3],["cover",2],["dust",6],["fog",2],["hide",2],["haze",6],["obscure",0]],"en":"By five in the morning a cold mist had covered the whole valley. A low cloud sat on the hills and seemed to overshadow every tree. Fine dust from the dry road hung in the air and made a grey haze. The old fog from the night before would hide the far bridge. We could only see a few steps ahead, and the wet glass began to obscure the signs. My brother drove slowly and kept the lights low. As the sun rose, the mist lifted and the road appeared again. We reached the top of the pass before breakfast.","zh":"早上五点，一层冷雾罩住了整个山谷。低云压在山头上，像是把每棵树都盖住了。干路上扬起的细尘浮在空中，成了一层灰蒙蒙的薄霭。夜里留下的浓雾遮住了远处的桥。我们只能看清前面几步，湿玻璃也开始把路牌弄得模模糊糊。哥哥开得很慢，车灯也调得很低。太阳升起时，雾散了，路又露了出来。早饭前我们到了山口。"},"murmur":{"tw":[["mutter",0],["coo",3],["sound",2],["shriek",6],["grumble",0],["talk",2],["growl",6],["croak",0]],"en":"All night a low murmur filled the hospital corridor outside the ward. Two nurses would talk in soft voices as they passed the beds. From a far room came the small sound of a sick child, more a coo than a cry. An old man began to mutter about the cold and the long wait. His neighbour would grumble about the food and then fall asleep again. Once a sharp shriek came from the yard, and we all looked up. Outside, a dog started to growl at a passing van, and a frog gave a single croak. By morning the corridor was quiet, and the light came in grey.","zh":"整整一夜，病房外那条走廊里都飘着一片低低的絮语。两个护士经过病床时会轻声说话。远处一间屋里传来生病孩子的细小声音，与其说是哭，不如说是轻哼。一位老人开始嘟囔着说冷，说等得太久。他旁边的人会抱怨饭菜，然后又睡过去。有一回院里传来一声尖利的尖叫，我们都抬起头。外面一条狗冲着路过的货车低吼，一只青蛙又咕地叫了一声。到早上，走廊静了，光灰蒙蒙地照进来。"},"navigate":{"tw":[["sail",0],["cruise",3],["travel",2],["configure",6],["pilot",0],["steer",2],["scour",6],["voyage",0]],"en":"Before dawn my uncle would navigate the small boat out of the bay. He liked to sail at night, when the water was calm and the wind low. His old pilot friend had taught him to steer by the stars alone. Now a small screen helped him configure the route before each voyage. They would travel for hours, then cruise slowly past the rocky point. When the fish were scarce, they had to scour a wider area for a good catch. By noon the baskets were full and the engine turned for home. He said the sea never lets you grow lazy.","zh":"天亮前，叔叔会把小船驶出海湾。他喜欢在夜里航行，那时水面平静、风也小。他那位老领航员朋友教过他单靠星星掌舵。如今一块小屏幕帮他在每次远航前设定好航线。他们会走上好几个钟头，再慢慢巡航过那片礁石滩。鱼少的时候，他们得在更大范围里搜寻好收成。中午篮子就满了，发动机掉头回家。他说，大海从不让你偷懒。"},"packet":{"tw":[["bundle",0],["deck",3],["boat",2],["filter",6],["parcel",0],["wisp",3],["message",2],["transmit",6]],"en":"In the little post room by the harbour, a packet of letters waited on the desk. My aunt would bundle them by street and filter out the heavy parcels. A brown parcel from a far port still carried the smell of the sea. Above the desk a wisp of smoke rose from the old stove. She would read each message, then transmit a short reply by phone. Outside, a fishing boat rocked near the deck of the pier. By noon the last packet was gone and the room was still. She sat down and drank her cold tea.","zh":"港口边那间小小的邮政房里，一捆信件等在桌上。我姑妈会按街道把它们扎起来，把沉包裹挑出去。一个从远方口岸寄来的棕色包裹还带着海的气味。桌上方的旧炉子里升起一缕烟。她会读每一封信，再用电话发一句简短的回话。外面，一条渔船在栈桥的甲板边晃着。到中午，最后一件包裹也发出去了，屋里静了下来。她坐下来喝那杯放凉的茶。"},"peel":{"tw":[["skin",0],["jacket",3],["chip",2],["lime",6],["strip",2],["rind",2],["ginger",6],["flake",0]],"en":"My grandmother would peel a lemon with a small knife in one long strip. She often left the thin rind on, because it held the best smell. Then she added a little ginger and a squeeze of lime to the mix. With a quick hand she would chip the hard skin off a piece of fruit. Her old jacket hung on the chair and smelled of spice and smoke. Once the pan was hot, she let a dry flake of dough fall in. The kitchen filled with a warm scent, and we lined up at the door. No one left the table until every plate was clean.","zh":"我奶奶会用一把小刀把柠檬削成一条长长的皮。她常常留着那层薄薄的外皮，因为香味都在那里。然后她会往里面加一点姜和几滴青柠汁。她手快，一下就削掉一块水果上那层硬皮。她那件旧外套搭在椅子上，闻着有香料和烟火的气味。锅一热，她就让一小片干面皮掉进去。厨房里弥漫起一股暖香，我们排着队在门口等着。盘子没吃干净，谁也不离开桌子。"},"pledge":{"tw":[["drink",2],["guarantee",3],["promise",2],["accept",6],["toast",0],["covenant",3],["raise",6],["subscribe",0]],"en":"At the end of the meeting every member had to make a small pledge. The chair asked us to promise one hour of help each week. To raise money for the old park, she hoped at least thirty people would subscribe. In return the town would guarantee free seeds for every family. Nobody had to accept the plan at once; they could think it over. Then we stood and shared a toast with a soft drink in our hands. The old covenant of the club, she said, was simply to keep our word. We left with the paper signed and a lighter heart.","zh":"会议结束时，每个成员都得许下一个小小的承诺。主席请大家保证每周帮一个钟头的忙。为了给老公园筹钱，她希望至少有三十个人来认捐。作为回报，镇上会保证每户人家都能领到免费的种子。谁都不必当场接受这个方案，可以先想一想。然后我们站起来，端着杯软饮料一起干了一杯。她说，这个俱乐部的老约定很简单，就是说话算数。我们拿着签好的纸离开，心里也轻快了些。"},"postpone":{"tw":[["table",0],["call",3],["delay",2],["cancel",6],["defer",0],["hold",3],["announce",6],["remit",0]],"en":"Because of the heavy rain, the committee chose to postpone the summer fair. The chair made a short call to the park office and asked them to hold the field. They could not cancel the event, only delay it by two weeks. On the table lay the old list of helpers and a long budget sheet. The secretary had to announce the new date to every stall. Some members wanted to defer the whole plan until next year. In the end they agreed to remit the fees to anyone who asked. The rain stopped by evening, and we all felt fine.","zh":"因为雨太大，委员会决定把夏季集市往后推。主席给公园办公室打了个短电话，请他们留着那块场地。他们不能取消，只能推迟两个星期。桌上摊着旧日的帮手名单和一页长长的预算。秘书得把新日子通知到每个摊位。有些成员想把整个计划拖到明年。最后大家同意给提出要求的人退钱。傍晚雨停了，我们也都觉得还行。"},"proclaim":{"tw":[["exalt",0],["hymn",3],["assert",2],["affirm",6],["laud",0],["declare",2],["reiterate",6],["promulgate",0]],"en":"On the first warm Sunday the whole village gathered to proclaim the new park open. An old singer led a hymn while the children stood in a row. The mayor would exalt the workers who had planted every tree. He had to assert that the land would stay free for all. Then he would declare the gate open with a single word. To affirm the promise, the council promised to protect the pond. Later they would reiterate the same plan in a short letter to every home. Some wanted to laud the donors and to promulgate the news in the paper. The band played, and the park filled with families.","zh":"第一个暖和的星期日，全村人聚在一起，宣布新公园开园。一位老歌手领唱了一首赞美诗，孩子们站成一排。镇长要表彰那些亲手栽下每棵树的人。他必须声明这片地会永远免费向所有人开放。接着他要说一句话，宣告大门开启。为了证实这个承诺，镇里保证会保护那个池塘。过后他们还会给每家每户写一封短信，重申同样的打算。有人想夸一夸那些捐助者，也提出把消息登到报纸上。乐队奏起来，公园里挤满了人家。"},"inflame":{"tw":[["heat",0],["ferment",3],["arouse",2],["provoke",6],["wake",0],["heighten",6],["ignite",2]],"en":"A careless word at the meeting was enough to inflame the whole room. The heat of the argument began to rise, and one member tried to provoke the other side. Nobody wanted to wake the old quarrel again. The chair let the talk ferment for a minute, then asked for calm. She knew that a sharp reply could arouse anger and heighten the tension. Her quiet voice seemed to ignite nothing at all, which was exactly her aim. In the end both sides agreed to wait a week. They left the hall slowly, without looking at each other.","zh":"会上的一句蠢话，就足以把满屋子人的火都点起来。争论的温度开始升高，有人还想去刺激对方。谁也不想再把旧账翻起来。主席让话先发酵了一分钟，然后请大家冷静。她知道，一句尖刻的回话会激起怒气、把紧张气氛推得更高。她那平静的声音好像什么也没点着，而这正是她的目的。最后双方同意等一个星期。他们慢慢走出大厅，谁也不看谁。"},"insult":{"tw":[["abuse",0],["indignity",3],["hurt",2],["shame",6],["affront",0],["disrespect",2],["excuse",6]],"en":"When the manager called the young worker lazy in front of everyone, the insult was clear. Such disrespect would hurt anyone, and it was a real affront to a man who had worked there for years. He felt a deep shame that he could not explain to his family. The manager later offered an excuse, but words of abuse cannot be taken back. The worker said the indignity of that morning would stay with him. He asked for a private talk and spoke without anger. In the end the manager said sorry, and meant it. The office learned something that day.","zh":"经理当着所有人说那个年轻工人懒，这明显是一种侮辱。这样的不尊重会伤到任何人，对一个在那儿干了多年的人来说，更是一种当众的冒犯。他心里有一份说不出口的羞耻，回家也没法对家人讲。后来经理给了个说法当借口，可辱骂的话是收不回来的。那工人说，那天早上所受的屈辱会一直跟着他。他要求单独谈一次，说话时没有带气。最后经理道了歉，而且是真心的。那天办公室学到了点东西。"},"invoke":{"tw":[["appeal",0],["bless",3],["request",2],["clause",6],["arouse",0],["plead",3],["evoke",0]],"en":"In court, the young lawyer chose to invoke an old clause of the housing law. She would appeal to the judge and plead for more time for her client. The written request sat on the desk, signed and dated. Her words seemed to arouse the interest of the whole room. She tried to evoke the cold nights her client had spent without heat. The judge listened and asked one sharp question. When he agreed, the family in the back row stood up. The old man said a quiet prayer to bless the court, and nobody stopped him.","zh":"在法庭上，那位年轻律师选择援引住房法里的一条旧条款。她要向法官陈情，为她的当事人争取更多时间。那份书面申请摆在桌上，签了名，注了日期。她的话似乎引起了满屋子人的兴趣。她试着让人想起她当事人那些没有暖气的寒夜。法官听着，问了一个很尖锐的问题。他答应之后，后排那一家人站了起来。老人轻声念了句祷词，为法庭祝福，没人拦他。"},"jerk":{"tw":[["buck",0],["move",2],["snatch",6],["flick",0],["pull",2],["tug",0]],"en":"With one quick jerk my father opened the stuck drawer of the old desk. The wood gave a small buck and then slid free. He had to pull the handle twice and snatch a folded paper from the back. A flick of his hand sent the dust into the air. Each tug on the drawer told him the rails were dry. He told me to move the desk away from the wet wall. Then he cut a thin strip of wood and fixed the runner. The drawer has opened smoothly ever since, and he still laughs about that morning.","zh":"我父亲猛地一拉，就把旧书桌那个卡住的抽屉拽开了。木头轻轻一弹，然后滑了出来。他得拉两下把手，从最里面抽出一张折着的纸。他手一弹，灰尘就飞了起来。每拉一下抽屉，他都能觉出滑轨是干的。他让我把桌子从潮湿的墙边挪开。然后他削了一根细木条，把滑道修好。从那以后，这抽屉一直开得很顺，他到现在还拿那天早上开玩笑。"},"limb":{"tw":[["arm",3],["leg",3],["edge",2],["jaw",6],["branch",2],["stick",3],["fracture",6]],"en":"During a walk in the hills, my brother hurt a limb on a sharp stone. He had tried to jump over a branch and landed badly on his leg. His arm was fine, but he could not put weight on the other side. A stick beside the path helped him hop back to the road. A doctor found a small fracture just above the ankle and told him to rest. His jaw was tight with pain, and he did not speak much. At the edge of the car park we waited for a friend to drive us home. He kept saying that the hill had won.","zh":"在山里散步时，我弟弟被一块尖石头伤到了一条腿脚。他想跳过一根树枝，结果那条腿落得很糟。胳膊没事，可另一条腿根本使不上劲。路边一根木棍帮他一路蹦回了大路。医生发现脚踝上方有一处小小的骨裂，让他休息。他疼得下巴咬得紧紧的，话也不多。我们在停车场的边上等一个朋友开车来接。他一直说，这座山赢了。"},"loom":{"tw":[["tower",0],["hang",2],["tangle",6],["hover",0],["look",2],["grapple",6],["brood",0]],"en":"For three weeks the final exam seemed to loom over the whole class. The results would tower above every other worry, and a heavy silence began to hang in the room. Our notes lay in a tangle on the desk, and nobody knew where to begin. A question we could not answer would hover in our minds all night. The teacher told us not to brood and to look at one small task at a time. She said we should grapple with the first page before we thought about the last. So we started, slowly. By the final morning, the fear had shrunk to something we could carry.","zh":"整整三个星期，期末考试像是压在整班人头上的阴影。成绩会高过其他所有烦心事，屋里开始挂上一片沉重的沉默。我们的笔记乱成一团摊在桌上，谁都不知道从哪儿下手。一个答不上来的问题会在脑子里悬一整夜。老师让我们别闷着想，一次只看一件小事。她说，应该先跟第一页较劲，再想最后一页。于是我们开始慢慢来。到了最后那个早上，那份恐惧已经缩小到我们背得动的程度。"},"mat":{"tw":[["flat",0],["change",2],["butt",6],["tangle",0],["mass",2],["strap",6],["snarl",0]],"en":"The old fisher sat on a flat mat at the door and worked on his net all morning. A great mass of line lay beside him in a tangle that looked hopeless. He would change his needle whenever the thread began to snarl. A leather strap held the net tight against his knee. Now and then he set the butt of his rod on the ground and rested. He said the sea gives no second chance to a careless hand. By noon the tangle was gone. He carried the net to the boat and hung it in the sun.","zh":"那位老渔夫坐在门口一张平整的席子上，整个上午都在补网。一大团线堆在他旁边，缠得像是没救了。只要线开始打结，他就换一根针。一条皮带把网紧紧压在他膝盖上。他时不时把鱼竿的粗头竖在地上歇一歇。他说，海从不给粗心的手第二次机会。到中午，那团乱线没了。他把网扛到船上，晾在太阳底下。"},"mediate":{"tw":[["middle",0],["lie",2],["immediate",1],["resolve",6],["arbitrate",0],["deadlock",6],["intermediate",5]],"en":"When two neighbours could not agree about the wall, a friend offered to mediate. She would sit in the middle of the room and let each side speak first. The truth, she said, usually lies somewhere between the two stories. There was no immediate answer, and for a while the talk reached a deadlock. She asked an older man to arbitrate the last point, since he owned the land between them. Little by little the two sides began to resolve their differences. An intermediate plan for the fence was written on paper. Both signed it that evening.","zh":"两家邻居为那堵墙谈不拢时，一位朋友主动出来调停。她会坐在屋子中间，让两边先各自把话说完。她说，真相通常就在两套说法之间的某处。这事没有立刻的答案，谈了一阵就僵住了。她请一位年长的人来仲裁最后一点，因为两家中间那块地是他的。慢慢地，两边开始化解分歧。一份折中的围栏方案写在了纸上。那天傍晚，两家都签了字。"},"odour":{"tw":[["smell",0],["bouquet",3],["sensation",2],["pungent",6],["scent",3],["stench",6],["aroma",3]],"en":"The moment I opened the door of the little shop, a warm odour of fresh bread filled my nose. Such an aroma could make anyone hungry. I could smell coffee from the back room and a sharp scent of orange peel. One jar gave off a pungent stench that was hard to forget. The owner said the bouquet of his old tea came from a long, slow drying. For me the whole room was a pleasant sensation, like a memory of my grandmother's kitchen. I bought bread and tea and a small bag of spice. On the way home I kept smelling the paper bag.","zh":"我一推开那家小店的门，一股热腾腾的新面包气味就扑满了鼻子。这样的香味能让任何人都饿。我能闻到里屋的咖啡味，还有一股柑橘皮的清香。有一个罐子散发出一股刺鼻的臭气，让人难忘。店主说，他那种老茶的香气来自长时间的慢烘。对我来说，整个屋子都是一种愉快的感受，像我奶奶厨房里的回忆。我买了面包、茶和一小袋香料。回家路上，我一直在闻那个纸袋。"},"oppress":{"tw":[["crush",0],["repress",3],["torment",2],["subjugate",6],["suppress",0],["purge",3],["terrify",6]],"en":"In the old factory the long night shifts began to oppress even the strongest workers. A hard manager would repress any complaint and try to suppress every honest talk. His sharp words could terrify a new hand on the first day. He seemed to enjoy the power to subjugate a whole team. One worker said the rules were heavy enough to crush a man's spirit. The union asked the company to purge the worst of those rules. Slowly the endless forms and the fear began to torment them less. By spring the night shift felt almost normal.","zh":"在那家老厂里，漫长的夜班开始压得住连最壮的工人都喘不过气。一个严厉的经理会压制任何抱怨，还想把真话全都堵住。他尖刻的话能让一个新来的第一天就吓住。他似乎很享受把整个小组压在手心里的那种权力。有个工人说，那些规矩重得能把一个人的精神压碎。工会要求公司清除最糟的那几条规矩。慢慢地，没完没了的表格和那种害怕，都不那么折磨人了。到春天，夜班几乎恢复正常了。"},"overlap":{"tw":[["lap",0],["share",3],["cover",2],["vary",6],["interface",3],["coincide",2],["originate",6]],"en":"Two small teams worked on the same project, and their tasks began to overlap. One group would cover the design while the other wrote the code. At the interface between them, several duties seemed to lap over each other. The manager asked them to share one list of tasks online. Ideas for the new app had to originate in the weekly meeting, so that plans would not vary too much. When two jobs coincide, she said, one of them must wait. The teams agreed on a simple rule. The work went faster after that, and nobody repeated another person's job.","zh":"两个小团队做着同一个项目，任务开始重叠。一组负责设计，另一组写代码。在两边交接的界面上，好几项活儿似乎互相搭在了一起。经理让他们在网上共用一份任务清单。新应用的点子必须在每周例会上产生，这样计划才不会差得太远。她说，两件事撞到一块儿时，其中一件就得等。大家定了一条简单的规矩。那以后活儿快多了，也没人重复别人干过的事。"},"parade":{"tw":[["march",2],["walk",2],["procession",6],["exhibit",0],["display",2],["festival",6],["troop",0]],"en":"Every year our town holds a small parade on the first warm day of spring. A long procession would march down the main street while the crowd stood on both sides. Older people walk slowly behind the band, and children run ahead. A troop of young dancers in bright cloth opened the festival that followed. Farmers came to exhibit their best fruit and to display old tools in the square. My aunt always watched from the same corner near the bridge. She said the noise was the sound of the town waking up. When the last cart passed, we all went home for lunch.","zh":"每年春天第一个暖和的日子，我们镇上都会办一场小小的游行。长长的队伍沿主街往前走，人群站在两边。年纪大的人跟在乐队后面慢慢走，孩子们跑在前头。一队穿亮色衣服的年轻舞者为随后的节庆开场。农民们来到广场，摆出最好的水果，展示旧式农具。我姑妈总在桥边同一个角落看。她说，那些喧闹就是小镇醒过来的声音。最后一辆大车过去后，我们都回家吃午饭了。"},"patent":{"tw":[["apparent",0],["change",2],["copyright",6],["plain",0],["register",2],["suit",6],["evident",0]],"en":"A young inventor from our street spent two years trying to register a patent for a simple water pump. The idea looked plain at first, yet it was apparent that the design could save a lot of work on a dry farm. It was evident that he had thought about every part. He also asked about a copyright for the small handbook he wrote. When a big company copied his pump, he brought a suit against them. The fight took a year and cost him a lot. In the end he won, but he had to change nothing. He still keeps the first drawing on his wall.","zh":"我们街上一个年轻的发明家花了两年，想为一个简单的水泵登记专利。这主意起初看着平平无奇，可很明显，这个设计能替干旱的农场省下许多工夫。看得出他对每个零件都想过。他还问了他那本小手册的版权问题。有家大公司仿造了他的水泵，他就把对方告上了法庭。这场官司打了一年，花了他不少钱。最后他赢了，可什么也不用改。他到现在还把那张最初的图纸挂在墙上。"},"patron":{"tw":[["sponsor",0],["host",3],["customer",2],["saint",6],["guarantor",3],["benefactor",2],["namesake",6]],"en":"The old reading room on our street was saved by a quiet patron who loved books. He had been a regular customer of the shop next door for forty years. As the main sponsor, he paid for new lamps and chairs out of his own pocket. A local bank agreed to act as guarantor of the rent for two years. Some people called him a benefactor, and one old woman said he was a saint. He only smiled and asked the host of the meeting to say nothing about it. His namesake, a nephew, helped him choose new books. The room opened again on a cold Saturday.","zh":"我们街上那间旧阅览室，被一位爱书的低调赞助人救了下来。四十年来，他一直是隔壁那家店的老主顾。作为主要赞助方，他自掏腰包买了新灯和新椅子。当地一家银行同意为两年的房租做担保人。有人称他恩人，一位老太太还说他是个圣人。他只是笑笑，请会议的主持人别提这件事。与他同名的小侄子帮他挑新书。一个冷飕飕的星期六，阅览室又开门了。"},"pearl":{"tw":[["bone",0],["white",2],["harbor",6],["drop",0],["gather",2],["dawn",6],["bead",0]],"en":"At dawn the small boats left the harbor and moved toward the open sea. My uncle worked on the deck with a thin white shell in his hand. He hoped to find one pearl inside, though he knew it was rare. The divers would gather at the rail and pass each shell up like a heavy bead. He told me that a single drop of sand can start the whole thing. By noon his hands were sore to the bone, and there was nothing to sell. Still he laughed and said the sea owed him nothing. We sailed home with an empty box and a good story.","zh":"天刚亮，小船就离开海港，驶向开阔的海面。我叔叔在甲板上干活，手里捏着一只薄薄的白贝壳。他希望里面能有一颗珍珠，尽管他知道这很罕见。潜水的人聚在栏杆边，把每只贝壳像一颗沉甸甸的珠子一样递上来。他告诉我，一粒沙子就能让整件事开始。到中午，他的手酸到骨头，却什么也没得卖。他还是笑着说，海不欠他什么。我们带着一只空箱子和一个好故事回了家。"},"prey":{"tw":[["feed",0],["victim",2],["predator",6],["target",0],["exploit",2],["shark",6],["quarry",0]],"en":"At the edge of the lake a heron stood still and watched its prey. A slow fish would soon become the victim of that long beak. This tall bird is a patient predator and never rushes its target. Men once tried to exploit the water for a factory, and the birds suffered. In the wide sea a small shark would feed on anything weak, but here the quarry was only a silver fish. My teacher asked us to write one page about hunters and their food. I chose the heron and watched it for an hour. It caught nothing, and I was happy for the fish.","zh":"湖边上，一只苍鹭静静站着，盯着它的猎物。一条游得慢的鱼很快就会成为那长喙的牺牲品。这高个子的鸟是个沉得住气的捕食者，从不急着扑向目标。人们曾想开发这片水域建厂，那些鸟就遭了殃。在广阔的海里，小鲨鱼会吃任何弱小的东西，可这里的猎物只是一条银色的鱼。老师让我们写一页关于捕食者和食物。我选了苍鹭，看了它一个钟头。它什么也没抓到，我倒替那条鱼高兴。"},"primitive":{"tw":[["rude",0],["savage",3],["word",2],["characteristic",6],["crude",0],["formula",2],["archaic",0]],"en":"In the history class we studied how primitive people made their first tools. The teacher said their crude stone knives looked rude to us, yet they were a great step. A savage hunt could mean the difference between eating and starving. The most interesting characteristic of that age was the slow growth of language. Every word for fire or water was a small invention. She wrote an old formula on the board and then an archaic sign beside it. We tried to copy both. That lesson made the past feel close, almost like a room next door.","zh":"历史课上，我们研究了原始人怎样做出最早的工具。老师说，他们那些粗糙的石刀在我们看来很粗陋，却是了不起的一步。一场凶狠的狩猎，意味着吃饱还是挨饿。那个时代最有趣的特点，是语言慢慢地生长起来。'火'或'水'的每一个词都是一次小小的发明。她在黑板上写下一个古老的公式，又在旁边写了一个古体的符号。我们照着描。那堂课让过去变得很近，几乎像隔壁的一间屋子。"},"proposition":{"tw":[["proffer",0],["particular",3],["offer",2],["measure",6],["touch",3],["propose",4],["repeal",6]],"en":"At the meeting the young manager made a short proposition about the new store. She would proffer a plan for a smaller shop and then wait for questions. Her first offer was to cut the rent for one particular street. She wanted to measure how many people walked past each day. The chair asked her to propose a clear date for the change. 'Let me touch on the cost,' she said, 'before we vote.' One member raised an old rule and asked to repeal it. In the end the vote passed, and the small shop opened in May.","zh":"会上，那位年轻经理就新店的事提了一个简短的提案。她先拿出一份开小店的方案，然后等着大家提问。她的第一个提议，是给某一条特定的街减租。她想量一量每天有多少人从那儿走过。主席让她提出一个明确的改动日期。她说，'投票之前，我先谈一下成本。'有位成员提了一条旧规定，要求把它废除。最后投票通过了，那家小店五月开张。"},"pulse":{"tw":[["beat",2],["move",2],["signal",6],["impulse",0],["rate",2],["sensor",6],["throb",3]],"en":"The nurse put a small sensor on the arm of the old man and watched the screen. His pulse was slow, and the beat of his heart came at an uneven rate. Every throb showed up as a line that would move across the display. She told me that a weak signal can look alarming even when nothing is wrong. The patient said he had felt one strange impulse in his chest the night before. We waited by the bed and counted each minute. By noon the numbers were steady again. He smiled and asked for tea.","zh":"护士在老人手臂上放了一个小传感器，盯着屏幕看。他的脉搏很慢，心跳的节律也不匀。每一下搏动都化成一条线，在屏幕上移动过去。她告诉我，一个微弱的信号看着吓人，其实什么事也没有。病人说，前一晚他胸口有过一阵奇怪的冲动。我们守在床边，数着每一分钟。到了中午，数字又稳了。他笑了笑，要喝茶。"},"ram":{"tw":[["drive",0],["toe",3],["stuff",2],["bang",6],["force",0],["sheep",2],["pound",0]],"en":"The old ram in the field had a heavy head and a bad temper. Farmers keep a ram with the sheep, but this one would drive anyone away from the gate. One morning it ran at the fence with a loud bang. The force of that hit made the whole line shake. My uncle hurt his toe while he tried to push the animal back. He said the ram could pound a wooden post into the ground. We moved the stuff in the yard and fixed the gate that night. Since then the sheep have kept to the far side.","zh":"地里那只老公羊脑袋沉、脾气坏。农人会把公羊和羊群养在一起，可这一只会把任何人从门口赶走。有天早上，它砰地一声撞在围栏上。那一下的力气让整排围栏都晃了。我叔叔想把它推回去，结果伤了脚趾。他说这只公羊能把一根木桩砸进地里。那天晚上我们把院子里的东西挪开，把门修好了。从那以后，羊群都躲到远远的那一头去了。"},"rap":{"tw":[["knock",3],["blow",2],["hop",6],["strike",2],["conversation",2],["pop",6],["blame",0]],"en":"A soft rap on the door woke me before the sun was up. I thought it was a knock from the neighbour, but nobody answered my call. Then a second blow came, harder, and I heard a small pop from the old heater. I had to hop out of bed and strike the switch with my hand. Outside, two men had stopped their conversation and were looking at the wall. They said the noise came from a loose pipe, not from me. I did not blame them for the early visit. We fixed it together before breakfast, and the day started well.","zh":"太阳还没出来，门上轻轻一下敲击就把我弄醒了。我以为是邻居在敲门，可我喊了一声没人应。接着又响了一下，更重，我还听见旧暖气发出一声小小的爆响。我只好跳下床，用手去砸那个开关。外面，两个男人停下聊天，正看着墙。他们说这响动是一根松了的管子发出来的，不是我的事。这么早来打扰，我并没有怪他们。早饭前我们一起把它修好了，这一天开头还算不错。"},"reconcile":{"tw":[["settle",0],["key",3],["adjust",2],["unite",6],["accommodate",0],["resolve",6],["resign",0]],"en":"After a long quarrel about money, my parents tried to reconcile their plans for the year. They had to settle the question of the old house and to adjust the family budget. The key to the whole problem, my mother said, was to talk before the anger grew. They decided to unite their two accounts into one. The bank could not accommodate every request, so some papers had to wait. In the end they found a way to resolve the last difficulty. My father agreed not to resign from his second job that spring. Since then, evenings at home have been calmer.","zh":"为钱吵了很久之后，我父母试着把两人这一年的打算调和起来。他们得把老房子的事定下来，还要调整家里的预算。我母亲说，整个问题的关键是趁气还没上来就先谈。他们决定把两个账户并成一个。银行没法满足每一个要求，所以有些材料只能等。最后他们找到了化解最后一个难题的办法。我父亲答应那年春天不辞掉第二份工作。从那以后，家里的晚上平静多了。"},"recur":{"tw":[["repeat",0],["cycle",3],["use",2],["transpire",6],["resort",0],["iterate",3],["arise",6]],"en":"The same fault would recur in our program every few weeks. We had to repeat the test many times before we understood it. The bug seemed to follow a slow cycle that no one could see. The only thing we could use was an old list of past errors. Our manager asked us to iterate the process until the pattern appeared. If a new problem should arise, he said, we would resort to the same careful steps. In time we learned what had transpired inside the machine. The fault has not come back since then, and we keep the notes.","zh":"同一个故障每隔几周就会在我们的程序里重现。我们把测试重复了很多遍才弄明白。这个漏洞似乎沿着一个谁也看不见的慢周期出现。我们唯一能用上的，是一份以前的错误清单。经理让我们把这个流程反复做，直到规律显出来。他说，要是再冒出新问题，我们就用同样的稳妥步骤。后来我们弄清了机器里到底发生了什么。那以后故障没再回来，我们一直留着那些记录。"},"refresh":{"tw":[["review",0],["vent",3],["change",2],["tire",1],["synchronize",6],["remember",2],["recharge",6]],"en":"By Friday afternoon the whole team was ready for a break to refresh their tired minds. We would review the week and then open a window to vent the warm air. A short walk could change the mood of everyone in the room. Our manager said a person who does not rest will soon tire and make mistakes. So we agreed to synchronize our lunch hour and to remember to leave on time. We also set a rule to recharge our laptops before the weekend. The office felt lighter after that. On Monday we worked better than we had in months.","zh":"到星期五下午，整个团队都想歇一歇，让疲乏的脑子清爽一下。我们先回顾这一周，再开窗把屋里的热气透出去。出去走一小段，就能改变屋里每个人的心情。我们经理说，不休息的人很快就会累，还会出错。于是我们说好把午饭时间统一起来，并且记得按时下班。我们还定了一条规矩：周末前把笔记本电脑充上电。那以后办公室轻松了不少。星期一，我们干得比过去几个月都好。"}}});
